    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and the full build reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented idempotent create for `POST /api/owners`: when a request repeats with an already-seen `Idempotency-Key`, the originally created owner is returned with **200** instead of creating a duplicate (which would otherwise 409).\n\nI added behaviour as small, cohesive new units rather than growing any existing class \u2014 every function I wrote has zero surrounding complexity (`WMC_other = 0`), and I left the existing pipeline functions (`BuildOwner`, `SaveOwner`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated`, \u2026) untouched.\n\n**New function classes** (each one small public method):\n- `IdempotencyStore` \u2014 a `@Component` holding a `ConcurrentMap<String,Integer>` (key \u2192 owner id).\n- `CheckIdempotencyKey` \u2014 new entry step. Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header; branches to the `replay` flow if the key is known, else the `create` flow.\n- `RespondWithReplayedOwner` \u2014 loads the remembered owner and responds 200.\n- `RecordIdempotencyKey` \u2014 after save, records the new owner under its key.\n\n**YAML wiring** (`owners.POST.yml`):\n- Added `idempotency` as the first step with two `outputs`: `create \u2192 build`, `replay \u2192 replayOwner`.\n- Inserted `recordIdempotency` between `save` and `respond` on the create path.\n\nThe create path is unchanged for requests without a key (the header is optional, `required=false` \u2192 null \u2192 normal flow). The replay path bypasses all the duplicate/quota checks entirely, so the repeat can't 409.",
