    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list for `POST /api/owners`, read straight from the pipeline in `owners.POST.yml` and the function classes it wires together.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n- **`hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`** \u2014 the file's `composition.authorize` guards the whole endpoint; a caller without the role never reaches the pipeline.\n\n## The pipeline (in wiring order)\n\n**1. `CheckIdempotencyKey`** *(entry step)*\n- Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header. If that key is already in the `IdempotencyStore`, it branches to `replay` \u2192 `RespondWithReplayedOwner` (re-fetches the previously created owner and returns it with **200**, running none of the steps below). Otherwise it branches to `create` and the create pipeline begins.\n\n**2. `BuildOwner`** *(this is where `@Valid @RequestBody` runs, so bean validation happens here \u2014 first)*\nValidations:\n- **Bean-validation on `OwnerFieldsDto`**: `firstName` NotNull + name-pattern + size 1\u201330; `lastName` NotNull + name-pattern (trailing `.` allowed) + size 1\u201330; `city` NotNull + size 1\u201380; `telephone` NotNull + pattern `^[-0-9+() ]*$` + size 1\u201320; `email` optional, `@Email` + max 255; `postcode` optional, pattern `^[0-9]{4}$`; `title` max 10; address fields size limits.\n- **`E164.normalize(telephone)`** \u2192 throws `InvalidTelephoneException` if the number can't be formed into 8\u201315 digits E.164, or the national-number length is wrong for the country code (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210).\n- **`AddressForm.apply`** \u2192 throws `AddressRequiredException` if neither the flat `address` nor `addressLine1` is supplied.\n- **Future-date check** \u2192 throws `FutureRegistrationDateException` if `registrationDate` is after today.\n\nSide-effects (mutations to the request/entity):\n- Overwrites `telephone` with its normalized E.164 form.\n- Normalizes the address: composes stored `address` from `addressLine1`(+` `+`addressLine2`) when structured fields are present, else normalizes the flat `address`.\n- Maps the DTO to a new `Owner` entity.\n- Defaults `registrationDate` to today when omitted.\n- **Rolls `registrationDate` forward** to the next business day (skips weekends and the 2026 holiday set).\n- Publishes a `sharesHousehold` boolean flag for later steps.\n\n**3. `EnsureOwnerEmailNotDisposable`** \u2014 validation: rejects (`DisposableEmailException`) if the email domain is in the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). No email \u2192 allowed.\n\n**4. `EnsureOwnerPostcodeWithinRegion`** \u2014 validation: if the owner has a postcode and its city maps to a region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), the postcode must fall in range, else `InvalidPostcodeException`. Unknown region or no postcode \u2192 allowed.\n\n**5. `EnsureOwnerIdentityUnique`** \u2014 validation: scans all non-deleted owners; if any has the same full `IdentityKey` (normalized telephone `|` email `|` householdId), throws `DuplicateIdentityException`.\n\n**6. `EnsureOwnerHouseholdUnique`** \u2014 validation: unless `sharesHousehold` is true, rejects (`DuplicateHouseholdException`) if any non-deleted owner shares the same `HouseholdId` (same normalized last name + postcode).\n\n**7. `EnsureOwnerCityWithinCapacity`** \u2014 validation: rejects (`CityAtCapacityException`) if the owner's city (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed) already holds **\u2265 50** owners.\n\n**8. `EnsureDailyOwnerLimitNotExceeded`** \u2014 validation: rejects (`DailyOwnerLimitException`) if **\u2265 100** existing owners already share the new owner's (business-day-adjusted) `registrationDate`.\n\n**9. `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`** \u2014 side-effect: sets `customerCode` to `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from `Locality`, plus first 8 hex of SHA-256 of `telephone + lastName`).\n\n**10. `DeduplicateOwnerCustomerCode`** \u2014 side-effect: if that code is already taken by another owner, appends `-<n>` with the smallest `n \u2265 2` that is unique.\n\n**11. `SaveOwner`** \u2014 side-effect: persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (assigns its id).\n\n**12. `RecordIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 side-effect: if an `Idempotency-Key` header was supplied, records `key \u2192 owner.id` in the `IdempotencyStore`.\n\n**13. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 side-effects and response:\n- Computes and sets on the DTO: `namesakeCount`, `membershipPoints`, `membershipLevel`, `bulkSignupWarning`, and `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`.\n- Writes an **AUDIT log** line (`owner created id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026 membershipLevel=\u2026 membershipNumber=\u2026`).\n- Sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the owner DTO body.\n\n## Transaction\n\nEvery step from `build` through `respond` carries `govern: [ transaction ]`, so all the reads, mutations, the save, and the idempotency record run inside **one transaction that commits once at the end** of the pipeline.\n\nOne note worth flagging: the `EnsureOwner\u2026` uniqueness/capacity checks filter on `!isDeleted()` (identity/household) but `EnsureOwnerCityWithinCapacity` and `EnsureDailyOwnerLimitNotExceeded` count *all* owners including soft-deleted ones \u2014 a real behavioral inconsistency, though you asked me only to report, not change it."
